  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the sacred temple ceremony the clan head wears ceremonial white robes and kneels on a brownish yellow floor before a tall black case of three layers that holds ancestor memorial tablets, with copper incense on both sides. Over ten elders and important members kneel behind him in the same fashion, wearing loose white ceremonial garments.",
      "chapters": [
        1
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moonlight Gu is the clan’s local Gu and a symbol of the clan. It is crystalline and shaped like a crescent, like a piece of blue quartz.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_moonlight_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The academy elder calls it the clan’s symbolic Gu, and to the clan’s youngsters it is the symbol of the clan’s glory.",
      "chapters": [
        22
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On alliance ground, Gu Yue Gu Masters are on the skinny side.",
      "chapters": [
        124
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hundreds of years earlier the clan migrated from the central lands to the South Border and settled after finding a spirit spring under the mountain, which becomes the foundation of Gu Yue Village.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_gu_yue_village"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A lightning wolf pack assaulting the village is a wolf tide that forces Gu Masters onto the walls through the night.",
      "chapters": [
        149
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Qing Mao Mountain also holds Flower Wine Monk’s strength inheritance. Chapter 60 is titled for the passage behind the broken wall, and the hideout behind the image wall is set to nurture an avenger against the Gu Yue clan.",
      "chapters": [
        60
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "inh_flower_wine_monk_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later underground, Fang Yuan is still inside that inheritance ground.",
      "chapters": [
        79
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three mountain villages sit there: Gu Yue, Xiong, and Bai.",
      "chapters": [
        65
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan already treats Bai and Xiong as the other two clan families on the mountain while the caravan is still in Gu Yue Village.",
      "chapters": [
        45
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three named arcs cover this stretch: Gu Yue Village, Qing Mao Mountain, and Gu Yue Clan Conflict.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "settlement-and-neighbours",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_arc_gu_yue_village",
        "evt_arc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "evt_arc_gu_yue_clan_conflict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The clan holds its Awakening Ceremony for fifteen-year-olds, and the distance a child walks during it reveals a talent grade from A to D.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "awakening-ceremony-and-clan-logic",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_awakening_ceremony"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Seven days later the academy treats those who opened their apertures as rank one Gu Masters. The grade follows a person afterwards: the protagonist is graded C beside an A grade twin on that basis.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "awakening-ceremony-and-clan-logic",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue Bo teaches that a clan is not just rules and regulations, but also blood relation and kinship. Rules alone leave a family a pile of dead objects; adding blood relationship makes it alive. He is the clan leader in the opening stretch.",
      "chapters": [
        58
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "awakening-ceremony-and-clan-logic",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_bo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Members carry the clan name before the personal name; chapter 140 titles a fight as “Gu Yue Qing Shu vs Bai Ning Bing (Part 1)”,",
      "chapters": [
        140
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "awakening-ceremony-and-clan-logic",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_qing_shu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and the novel later uses the same construction for the protagonist.",
      "chapters": [
        1673
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "awakening-ceremony-and-clan-logic",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan is inside this clan as Gu Yue Fang Yuan in the opening stretch, reborn five hundred years earlier by Spring Autumn Cicada.",
      "chapters": [
        1
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "who-the-clan-produces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng is his younger twin brother of the same generation.",
      "chapters": [
        2
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "who-the-clan-produces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The academy names him Gu Yue Fang Zheng among the newly awakened rank one Gu Masters,",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "who-the-clan-produces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "and he later fights as the clan’s rising junior on Qing Mao Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        83
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "who-the-clan-produces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue Qing Shu faces Bai Ning Bing in a rank three-scale fight across three consecutive chapter titles.",
      "chapters": [
        140
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "who-the-clan-produces",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 180 restages the Awakening Ceremony through a Photo-audio Gu imprint smashed open for investigation.",
      "chapters": [
        180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_photo_audio_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The protagonist’s next rebirth in this stretch comes when he forces the Spring Autumn Cicada again.",
      "chapters": [
        196
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deeper than the spirit spring sits the blood pond graveyard, the forbidden ground that buried the first generation’s coffin. Chapter 182 is titled “Blood pond graveyard”.",
      "chapters": [
        182
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 185 is titled “Gu Yue first gen, Five great flying zombies”. Under that title the first-generation clan head rises from the blood lake as a blood wight flying zombie, having used rank five Blood Wight Gu to bury himself there. The “five great flying zombies” names a set of zombie types that includes the blood wight, not five Gu Yue corpses under the pond.",
      "chapters": [
        185
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_first_gen_gu_yue",
        "gu_blood_wight_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 194 is titled “Blood Curtain Skyflower”. Under that title First gen Gu Yue names Blood Curtain Skyflower Gu as his personally fused rank five defense, stronger than rank four Water Curtain Skyflower Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        194
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_blood_curtain_skyflower_gu",
        "gu_water_curtain_skyflower_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 219 is titled “Entering Bai Gu mountain”, which opens the Bai Gu Mountain arc.",
      "chapters": [
        219
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_bai_gu_mountain",
        "evt_arc_bai_gu_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Shortly after, an investigative report claims Qing Mao Mountain’s three clans were completely wiped out and that Gu Yue remnants were under investigation.",
      "chapters": [
        220
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-conflict-and-exit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 334 is titled “Immortal Crane Sect, Fang Zheng”. In that chapter Fang Zheng appears inside Immortal Crane Sect in Central Continent, fights in the sect examination, and becomes an elite disciple.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
